     <w:jc w:val="both"/>
    </w:pPr>
    <w:r>
     <w:t>The interrupt status register has the status for each event that may be responsible for the generation of an interrupt to the corresponding user .</w:t>
    </w:r>
   </w:p>
   <w:p>
    <w:pPr>
     <w:spacing w:before="120"/>
     <w:ind w:first-line="720"/>
     <w:jc w:val="both"/>
     <w:spacing w:before="120"/>
     <w:ind w:first-line="0"/>
     <w:jc w:val="both"/>
    </w:pPr>
    <w:r>
     <w:t>Software may also write 1 to a given bit to set this bit to test interrupt generation. It will activate the status bit for two cycles. This may still be masked, however. Write 0 has no effect.</w:t>
    </w:r>
   </w:p>
