       <aml:annotation aml:id="0" w:type="Word.Bookmark.Start" w:name="_5872597a705bd27c"/>
       <aml:annotation aml:id="0" w:type="Word.Bookmark.End"/>
       <w:r>
        <w:t>FLOWRT[a]_INT_SRC (Interrupt Source), (0x49000000+(a*0x2000)+0x100), a=0..199</w:t>
       </w:r>
      </w:p>
   <w:p>
    <w:pPr>
     <w:spacing w:before="120"/>
     <w:ind w:first-line="720"/>
     <w:jc w:val="both"/>
     <w:spacing w:before="120"/>
     <w:ind w:first-line="0"/>
     <w:jc w:val="both"/>
    </w:pPr>
    <w:r>
     <w:t>The Interrupt Source  shows which of the rings that share the same interrupt as the current ring is setting the interrupt. This register will be the same for all the flows with the same aggregator. The bits are assigned based on the lowest flow number for the aggregator will be in bit 0 and each incremental above will be the next bit. So, if flows 5-10 share an interrupt then if flow 5 has a non-zero Masked Cause Register bit 0 will be set. If a ring does not have an interrupt then only bit 0 will be used.</w:t>
    </w:r>
   </w:p>
   <w:p>
    <w:pPr>
     <w:keepNext/>
    </w:pPr>
   </w:p>
