       <w:r>
        <w:t>FLOWRT[a]_BA_LO (Ring Base Address Lo Register Aliased), (0x49200000+(a*0x2000)+0x40), a=0..200</w:t>
       </w:r>
      </w:p>
   <w:p>
    <w:pPr>
     <w:spacing w:before="120"/>
     <w:ind w:first-line="720"/>
     <w:jc w:val="both"/>
     <w:spacing w:before="120"/>
     <w:ind w:first-line="0"/>
     <w:jc w:val="both"/>
    </w:pPr>
    <w:r>
     <w:t>The Ring Base Address Lo Register contains the 32 LSBs of the base address for the ring which is used to hand off pending work for the channel from the Host. The base address must be aligned to 0x8. A write to this register will reset the associated ring to clear the occupancies and reset the pointers. This register is an aliased version from the flow configuration register and is only visible if the alias bit is set in the RESRC register.</w:t>
    </w:r>
   </w:p>
   <w:p>
    <w:pPr>
