        <w:jc w:val="center"/>
        <w:keepNext/>
       </w:pPr>
      <w:r>
       <w:t>0x0</w:t>
      </w:r>
      </w:p>
     </w:tc>
     <w:tc>
      <w:p>
       <w:pPr>
        <w:ind w:left="30" w:right="0"/>
        <w:keepNext/>
       </w:pPr>
      <w:r>
       <w:t>Specifies whether or not the channel should immediately return a teardown completion response to the default completion queue or wait until a status message is returned from the remote PSI-L paired peripheral.  0 = return immediately once all traffic is complete in BCDMA.  1 = wait until remote peer sends back a completion message. This field is only valid if the channel is for a TX peripheral otherwise it is reserved. It is assumed that if the TX peripheral sends a tdown completion message it also sends EOP completion messages. Setting this bit enables delaying of TX completion events until the EOP completion message is received as well.</w:t>
      </w:r>
      </w:p>
     </w:tc>
    </w:tr>
    <w:tr>
     <w:tc>
