       <aml:annotation aml:id="0" w:type="Word.Bookmark.Start" w:name="_ae85315393ff3a20"/>
       <aml:annotation aml:id="0" w:type="Word.Bookmark.End"/>
       <w:r>
        <w:t>CHAN[a]_FIFO_DEPTH (Tx Channel FIFO Depth Register), (0x48190000+(a*0x100)+0x70), a=0..200</w:t>
       </w:r>
      </w:p>
   <w:p>
    <w:pPr>
     <w:spacing w:before="120"/>
     <w:ind w:first-line="720"/>
     <w:jc w:val="both"/>
     <w:spacing w:before="120"/>
     <w:ind w:first-line="0"/>
     <w:jc w:val="both"/>
    </w:pPr>
    <w:r>
     <w:t>The fifo depth register is used to specify how many FIFO data phases deep the Tx per channel FIFO will be for the channel.  While the maximum depth of the Tx FIFO is set at design time, the FIFO depth can be artificially reduced in order to control the maximum latency which can be introduced due to buffering effects. This register only exists if this channel is a TX peripheral channel otherwise it is reserved.</w:t>
    </w:r>
   </w:p>
   <w:p>
    <w:pPr>
     <w:keepNext/>
    </w:pPr>
   </w:p>
