       <w:r>
        <w:t>CHANRT[a]_THRD_ID (Channel Destination ThreadID Mapping Register Aliased), (0x48900000+(a*0x1000)+0x68), a=0..200</w:t>
       </w:r>
      </w:p>
   <w:p>
    <w:pPr>
     <w:spacing w:before="120"/>
     <w:ind w:first-line="720"/>
     <w:jc w:val="both"/>
     <w:spacing w:before="120"/>
     <w:ind w:first-line="0"/>
     <w:jc w:val="both"/>
    </w:pPr>
    <w:r>
     <w:t>The thread ID mapping register is used to pair the DMA channel to a specific destination thread.  All traffic generated from this channel will be sent with a thread_id on the PSI-L interface with the value from this register. This register is only valid if the channel is a TX or RX peripheral channel. This register is only visible if the alias cfg bit is set in the Channel Resource Register.</w:t>
    </w:r>
   </w:p>
   <w:p>
    <w:pPr>
     <w:keepNext/>
    </w:pPr>
   </w:p>
