     </w:tc>
     <w:tc>
      <w:p>
       <w:pPr>
        <w:ind w:left="30" w:right="0"/>
        <w:keepNext/>
       </w:pPr>
      <w:r>
       <w:t>Normally, when the Z count of FIFO operations has been reached, the Peripheral will close the packet with an end of packet indication going to either the next packet or TR. When this flag is set, the peripheral will instead trigger an end of line at the completion of Z which will make the receiving TR increment the ICNT1 but remain in the same TR.</w:t>
      </w:r>
      </w:p>
     </w:tc>
    </w:tr>
    <w:tr>
