     <aml:annotation aml:id="0" w:type="Word.Bookmark.Start" w:name="_MMR_Region__par_dmss__pktdma0_cfg__flow"/>
     <aml:annotation aml:id="0" w:type="Word.Bookmark.End"/>
     <w:r>
      <w:t>MMR Region: par_dmss__pktdma0_cfg__flow</w:t>
     </w:r>
    </w:p>
   <w:p>
    <w:pPr>
     <w:spacing w:before="120"/>
     <w:ind w:first-line="720"/>
     <w:jc w:val="both"/>
     <w:spacing w:before="120"/>
     <w:ind w:first-line="0"/>
     <w:jc w:val="both"/>
    </w:pPr>
    <w:r>
     <w:t>The PKTDMA Ring Control / Status Registers region is accessed by setting the cfg_rsel signal to 3 during the access.  This region is sparsely populated based on the flows used. The addressing is per flow and the flow number for the specific register should be determined by the channel map for the DMA along with the number of flows supported by the channel. The channel number associated with the flow is always the smallest flow number supported. Each flow is seperated by a stride of 0x100. The address map for this region is as follows:</w:t>
    </w:r>
   </w:p>
     <wx:sub-section>
     <w:p>
      <w:pPr>
       <w:pStyle w:val="Heading3"/>
