      </wx:sub-section>
      <wx:sub-section>
      <w:p>
       <w:pPr>
        <w:pStyle w:val="Heading4"/>
        <w:listPr>
         <wx:t wx:val="4.87.2.32" wx:wTabBefore="0" wx:wTabAfter="180"/>
         <wx:font wx:val="Arial"/>
        </w:listPr>
        <w:keepNext/>
       </w:pPr>
       <aml:annotation aml:id="0" w:type="Word.Bookmark.Start" w:name="_5c431916cefe25e4"/>
       <aml:annotation aml:id="0" w:type="Word.Bookmark.End"/>
       <w:r>
        <w:t>CHANRT[a]_STATIC_TR_Z (0x4c000000+(a*0x1000)+0x804), a=0..255</w:t>
       </w:r>
      </w:p>
   <w:p>
    <w:pPr>
     <w:spacing w:before="120"/>
     <w:ind w:first-line="720"/>
     <w:jc w:val="both"/>
     <w:spacing w:before="120"/>
     <w:ind w:first-line="0"/>
     <w:jc w:val="both"/>
    </w:pPr>
    <w:r>
     <w:t>After reset, all channels in the PDMA will be idle and waiting for work to be assigned to them.  In order to initiate DMA operation on a peripheral, the Host will set up the static TR for the peripheral side of the channel. The format of the TR is identical for each DMA mode, consisting of an X, Y, and Z parameter, but the field interpretation varies based on the peripheral this register holds the Z parameters. This register is only on RX channels that send data from the PDMA to the Paired DMA</w:t>
    </w:r>
   </w:p>
   <w:p>
    <w:pPr>
     <w:keepNext/>
    </w:pPr>
   </w:p>
