       </w:pPr>
      <w:r>
       <w:t>This register contains the number of bytes that have been accessed from the VBUSP mapped peripheral. The register is write to decrement, so running counts can be tracked by reading register and then writing back the value that was read. It will wrap on overflow. It will reset to zero on a channel reset.</w:t>
      </w:r>
